cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sanket or build on it, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Sanket: AI-based detection of medium-range weather forecast busts across India"
abstract: >-
  Sanket predicts the probability that a medium-range weather forecast will bust (its
  error landing above the 90th percentile of that variable's own historical errors) for
  each of India's 666 districts, eight surface variables and lead days 1 to 10, and
  explains every prediction with SHAP. It is trained on NOAA GEFSv12 ensemble reforecasts
  verified against ERA5, compared against a ladder of statistical baselines on held-out
  years, and served at zero hosting cost. Built for Smart India Hackathon 2026, problem
  statement SIH26079 (Ministry of Earth Sciences).
authors:
  - name: "Team Winging It"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Bhushan2318/sih-main"
url: "https://sanket-a0dd.onrender.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
